msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A quantum-classical workflow runs as one managed workflow job. Its classical stages run on your compute profile, and the primitive jobs that it sends to an IBM Quantum&reg; QPU run on your instance and count against your usage. From that one job, you can report each stage, find the QPU jobs, and cancel them. To start a job and check its status and logs, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Ang isang quantum-classical workflow ay tumatakbo bilang isang managed workflow job. Ang mga classical stage nito ay tumatakbo sa iyong compute profile, at ang mga primitive job na ipinapadala nito sa isang IBM Quantum&reg; QPU ay tumatakbo sa iyong instance at kasama sa iyong usage. Mula sa iisang job na iyon, maaari mong i-report ang bawat stage, hanapin ang mga QPU job, at kanselahin ang mga ito. Para magsimula ng job at tingnan ang status at mga log nito, tingnan ang [Magpatakbo ng managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin, [deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Bago ka magsimula, [i-deploy ang una mong managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the Runtime service {#create-the-runtime-service}"
msgstr "Gawin ang Runtime service {#create-the-runtime-service}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the Runtime service in your workflow code with `get_runtime_service()`, and use it in the same way that you use `QiskitRuntimeService` locally. The following workflow runs a Bell circuit with the Sampler primitive, reports each stage with `update_status()`, and returns the counts:\n"
msgstr "Gawin ang Runtime service sa code ng workflow mo gamit ang `get_runtime_service()`, at gamitin ito tulad ng paggamit mo sa `QiskitRuntimeService` nang local. Nagpapatakbo ang sumusunod na workflow ng Bell circuit gamit ang Sampler primitive, nire-report ang bawat stage gamit ang `update_status()`, at ibinabalik ang mga count:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_runtime_service()` returns a `QiskitRuntimeService` that is set up for your managed workflow job, and it provides the following:\n"
msgstr "Ang `get_runtime_service()` ay nagbabalik ng `QiskitRuntimeService` na naka-set up para sa managed workflow job mo, at ibinibigay nito ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Credentials.** The Runtime service uses the API key, instance, and channel that you used to call `run()`, so the workflow code needs no credentials.\n"
msgstr "**Mga credential.** Ginagamit ng Runtime service ang API key, instance, at channel na ginamit mo sa pagtawag ng `run()`, kaya hindi kailangan ng code ng workflow ng mga credential.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Tracking.** A workflow records every primitive job that runs through this Runtime service under the managed workflow job, including Sampler, Estimator, and Executor jobs, and jobs in a session or batch. You can list them with `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "**Pag-track.** Nire-record ng isang workflow ang bawat primitive job na tumatakbo sa Runtime service na ito sa ilalim ng managed workflow job, kasama ang mga Sampler, Estimator, at Executor job, at mga job sa isang session o batch. Maaari mong ilista ang mga ito gamit ang `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cancellation.** When you call `job.cancel()`, the managed workflow also cancels the workflow's sessions, batches, and primitive jobs that are still running.\n"
msgstr "**Pagkansela.** Kapag tinawag mo ang `job.cancel()`, kinakansela rin ng managed workflow ang mga session, batch, at primitive job ng workflow na tumatakbo pa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow does not track or cancel the jobs of a service that you create with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, although the jobs still run. If the workflow must use another service, cancel its jobs in a [`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"
msgstr "Hindi tina-track o kinakansela ng managed workflow ang mga job ng service na ginawa mo gamit ang `QiskitRuntimeService()`, bagaman tumatakbo pa rin ang mga job. Kung kailangang gumamit ng ibang service ang workflow, kanselahin ang mga job nito sa isang [`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run primitives in a session or batch {#run-primitives-in-a-session-or-batch}"
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng mga primitive sa isang session o batch {#run-primitives-in-a-session-or-batch}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow also tracks primitive jobs that run in a session or batch. Create the session or batch from a backend that the Runtime service returned, and create the primitives inside the `with` block. `Session` works in the same way:\n"
msgstr "Tina-track din ng managed workflow ang mga primitive job na tumatakbo sa isang session o batch. Gawin ang session o batch mula sa isang Backend na ibinalik ng Runtime service, at gawin ang mga primitive sa loob ng `with` block. Ganito rin gumagana ang `Session`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report progress with update_status() {#report-progress-with-update_status}"
msgstr "Mag-report ng progress gamit ang update_status() {#report-progress-with-update_status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow in [Create the Runtime service](#create-the-runtime-service) calls `update_status()` at the start of each stage, so that the job status shows where the workflow is, such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. Pass one of the following `Job` constants:\n"
msgstr "Tinatawag ng workflow sa [Gawin ang Runtime service](#create-the-runtime-service) ang `update_status()` sa simula ng bawat stage, para ipakita ng status ng job kung nasaan ang workflow, gaya ng `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. Magpasa ng isa sa mga sumusunod na `Job` constant:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Call in the workflow | Job status |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.MAPPING)` | `RUNNING: MAPPING` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` | `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.WAITING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.EXECUTING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.POST_PROCESSING)` | `RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Tawag sa workflow | Status ng job |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.MAPPING)` | `RUNNING: MAPPING` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` | `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.WAITING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.EXECUTING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.POST_PROCESSING)` | `RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`update_status()` returns `True` if the workflow changed the status. It returns `False` and writes a warning to the logs if the value is not one of these constants, if the job is no longer active, or if the code runs outside a job. It does not raise an error, so a typo does not stop the workflow.\n"
msgstr "Ang `update_status()` ay nagbabalik ng `True` kung binago ng workflow ang status. Nagbabalik ito ng `False` at nagsusulat ng babala sa mga log kung ang value ay hindi isa sa mga constant na ito, kung hindi na aktibo ang job, o kung tumatakbo ang code sa labas ng job. Hindi ito nagtataas ng error, kaya hindi pinipigilan ng typo ang workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For progress within a stage, such as the iterations of an optimizer, [write log lines](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-decide-what-to-log).\n"
msgstr "Para sa progress sa loob ng isang stage, gaya ng mga iteration ng isang optimizer, [magsulat ng mga log line](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-decide-what-to-log).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: each update_status() call writes a SUB_STATUS_CHANGE event, and the 24-hour timeout is measured from the job's latest event (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py _timed_out). send_error() events count too. This looks like a bug; do not document it until the intended behavior is confirmed. */}\n"
msgstr ""

