# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `job` object exists only in the notebook that started the run. In a new notebook, get the job again with `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")`, then call `runtime_jobs()` on it. See [Find a job from a new session](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"
msgstr "Ang `job` object ay umiiral lang sa notebook na nagsimula ng run. Sa bagong notebook, kunin muli ang job gamit ang `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")`, saka tawagin ang `runtime_jobs()` dito. Tingnan ang [Hanapin ang job mula sa bagong session](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the QPU usage and run times of each QPU job, see [View job metrics](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). For the usage of your whole instance in the current period, call `client.usage()`. To see how long each stage of the managed workflow job took, see [Check how long each stage took](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"
msgstr "Para sa QPU usage at mga run time ng bawat QPU job, tingnan ang [Tingnan ang mga metric ng job](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). Para sa usage ng buong instance mo sa kasalukuyang period, tawagin ang `client.usage()`. Para makita kung gaano katagal ang bawat stage ng managed workflow job, tingnan ang [Tingnan kung gaano katagal ang bawat stage](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel linked QPU jobs {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"
msgstr "Kanselahin ang mga naka-link na QPU job {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a managed workflow job with `job.cancel()`, the workflow also tries to cancel the QPU work that the workflow started:\n"
msgstr "Kapag kinansela mo ang isang managed workflow job gamit ang `job.cancel()`, sinusubukan din ng workflow na kanselahin ang QPU work na sinimulan ng workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions and batches.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's sessions and batches, which also cancels their queued jobs.\n"
msgstr "**Mga session at batch.** Kinakansela ng workflow ang bawat session at batch ng workflow, na kinakansela rin ang mga naka-queue nilang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other primitive jobs.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's other primitive jobs that are still queued or running.\n"
msgstr "**Iba pang primitive job.** Kinakansela ng workflow ang bawat iba pang primitive job ng workflow na naka-queue o tumatakbo pa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message for each QPU job and session, so you can check what was canceled:\n"
msgstr "Ang `job.cancel()` ay nagbabalik ng mensahe para sa bawat QPU job at session, para masuri mo kung ano ang nakansela:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a workflow that ran in a batch, the message looks like the following:\n"
msgstr "Para sa workflow na tumakbo sa isang batch, ganito ang hitsura ng mensahe:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the client cannot create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, it cancels only the managed workflow job. Cancel the QPU jobs yourself with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Kung hindi makagawa ang client ng `QiskitRuntimeService` mula sa mga local mong credential, ang managed workflow job lang ang kakanselahin nito. Kanselahin mo mismo ang mga QPU job gamit ang mga ID nila mula sa `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a workflow stops a job itself, for example because it reached the 24-hour limit, it does not cancel its QPU jobs. Cancel them with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Kapag ang workflow mismo ang nagpatigil ng job, halimbawa dahil umabot ito sa 24-oras na limitasyon, hindi nito kinakansela ang mga QPU job nito. Kanselahin ang mga ito gamit ang mga ID nila mula sa `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the scheduler's timeout and blocked-account stops (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout, FleetsJobCanceller) cancel only the fleet. Only the user stop endpoint (StopJobUseCase) cancels runtime jobs. Confirm whether this is intended before publishing. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot QPU jobs in a workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Mag-troubleshoot ng mga QPU job sa isang workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` raises `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | The code runs in your local notebook, not in a managed workflow job. Use `QiskitRuntimeService()` locally. |\n"
"| `update_status()` returns `False`, and the logs show `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | The value is not one of the `Job` constants, or the job is no longer active. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` returns `[]`. | The workflow created its service with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, or it has not run a primitive yet. |\n"
"| A session's jobs are not tracked. | The session was created from a backend of a different service. Get the backend from `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| The workflow logs show `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | The workflow could not record a primitive job. The primitive job still runs, but it is not tracked. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` shows `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | The client could not create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, so it canceled only the managed workflow job. |\n"
"| `client.job()` fails with `Job [...] not found`. | The job ID is wrong, or the job belongs to another user. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Sanhi |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Nagtataas ang `get_runtime_service()` ng `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | Tumatakbo ang code sa local mong notebook, hindi sa managed workflow job. Gamitin ang `QiskitRuntimeService()` nang local. |\n"
"| Nagbabalik ang `update_status()` ng `False`, at ipinapakita ng mga log ang `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | Ang value ay hindi isa sa mga `Job` constant, o hindi na aktibo ang job. |\n"
"| Nagbabalik ang `job.runtime_jobs()` ng `[]`. | Ginawa ng workflow ang service nito gamit ang `QiskitRuntimeService()`, o wala pa itong napapatakbong primitive. |\n"
"| Hindi tina-track ang mga job ng isang session. | Ginawa ang session mula sa Backend ng ibang service. Kunin ang Backend mula sa `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| Ipinapakita ng mga log ng workflow ang `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | Hindi ma-record ng workflow ang isang primitive job. Tumatakbo pa rin ang primitive job, pero hindi ito tina-track. |\n"
"| Ipinapakita ng `job.cancel()` ang `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | Hindi nakagawa ang client ng `QiskitRuntimeService` mula sa mga local mong credential, kaya ang managed workflow job lang ang kinansela nito. |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang `client.job()` na may `Job [...] not found`. | Mali ang job ID, o ang job ay pag-aari ng ibang user. |\n"

